  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0c9baa00-cafd-57b9-b8f5-fdc90c420690" activityNameId="23702b79-5fbf-5a72-acfc-3eed0d2607b1" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Chlorine, gaseous, membrane cell, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Chlorine, gaseous, membrane cell, at plant
The multioutput-process "chlor-alkali electrolysis, membrane cell" delivers the co-products "chlorine, gaseous, membrane cell, at plant", "sodium hydroxide, 50% in water, membrane cell, at plant" and "hydrogen, liquid, membrane cell, at plant". The allocation is done according to the masses of the different products - i.e. 46.4% chlorine - 52.3% sodium hydroxide and 1.3% hydrogen.;
UUID: 8d48acd2-f507-38c2-984b-a0820f3305ff
Besides the electrolysis process in a membrane cell, the following process steps are included into this process: brine production, brine purification, brine resaturation as well as the final handling of the electrolysis products, without - the chlorine liquifaction!
Location: European average values
Technology: present state of technology used in european membrane cells
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Average values from the ranges indicated in EC IPPC-BAT document are used 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8d48acd2-f507-38c2-984b-a0820f3305ff.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
